      "tag": "AI动态",
      "tagClass": "tag-neutral",
      "fullContent": "X.PIN on X: \"The NSA, FBI and CISA accused DeepSeek, Moonshot AI, Alibaba, MiniMax, StepFun and https://t.co/eXv6hK3OVa of extracting knowledge from US models at industrial scale since at least 2024.\nThe agencies allege they routed requests through multiple channels to bypass rules and improve mat… / X Post\nLog in Sign up\nPost\nX.PIN on X: \"The NSA, FBI and CISA accused DeepSeek, Moonshot AI, Alibaba, MiniMax, StepFun and https://t.co/eXv6hK3OVa of extracting knowledge from US models at industrial scale since at least 2024.\nThe agencies allege they routed requests through multiple channels to bypass rules and improve math and coding. Distillation is legitimate when authorized; the dispute centers on access and consent.\nUS developers were urged to act immediately and share intelligence. The companies did not immediately comment.\"\nX.PIN\n@thexpin\nThe NSA, FBI and CISA accused DeepSeek, Moonshot AI, Alibaba, MiniMax, StepFun and Z.ai of extracting knowledge from US models at industrial scale since at least 2024.\nThe agencies allege they routed requests through multiple channels to bypass rules and improve math and coding. Distillation is legitimate when authorized; the dispute centers on access and consent.\nUS developers were urged to act immediately and share intelligence. The companies did not immediately comment.\n9:20 · 2026年9月9日 580 Views\n1\nX.PIN\n@thexpin\nThe NSA, FBI and CISA accused DeepSeek, Moonshot AI, Alibaba, MiniMax, StepFun and Z.ai of extracting knowledge from US models at industrial scale since at least 2024.\nThe agencies allege they routed requests through multiple channels to bypass rules and improve math and coding. Distillation is legitimate when authorized; the dispute centers on access and consent.\nUS developers were urged to act immediately and share intelligence. The companies did not immediately comment.\n9:20 · 2026年9月9日 580 Views\n1"
