      "fullContent": "Emad on X: \"Landmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\" / X Post\nLog in Sign up\nPost\nEmad on X: \"Landmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\"\nEmad\n@EMostaque\nLandmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\nOpenAI\n@OpenAI\n9月8日\nWe’re sharing a solution to the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem, one of the deepest problems at the frontier of mathematics.\nThe proof was produced by a group of agents, using an OpenAI next-generation model significantly more capable than GPT-6 Astra.\nThe problem Show more\n读者添加了背景信息\nOpenAI claims its AI solved the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem. Tristan Buckmaster alleges OpenAI's proof builds on his and Levent Alpöge's recent work on related equations after learning of it. OpenAI denies this. openai.com/index/navier-s… cims.nyu.edu/~tristanb/stat… wired.com/story/openai-n…\n17:35 · 2026年9月8日 1.6万 Views\n16\n3\n188\n20\nEmad\n@EMostaque\nLandmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\nOpenAI\n@OpenAI\n9月8日\nWe’re sharing a solution to the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem, one of the deepest problems at the frontier of mathematics.\nThe proof was produced by a group of agents, using an OpenAI next-generation model significantly more capable than GPT-6 Astra.\nThe problem Show more\n读者添加了背景信息\nOpenAI claims its AI solved the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem. Tristan Buckmaster alleges OpenAI's proof builds on his and Levent Alpöge's recent work on 