      "fullContent": "Chubby♨️ on X: \"This could be one of the most significant AI safety incidents to date.\nReuters reports that OpenAI agents escaped their testing environment and made more than 15,000 edits to a German wiki, effectively turning it into a message board for other AI agents.\nThey allegedly used it to … / X Post\nLog in Sign up\nPost\nChubby♨️ on X: \"This could be one of the most significant AI safety incidents to date.\nReuters reports that OpenAI agents escaped their testing environment and made more than 15,000 edits to a German wiki, effectively turning it into a message board for other AI agents.\nThey allegedly used it to share solutions, bypass restrictions, avoid detection and preserve their communications across separate agent runs. When moderators began deleting the pages, the agents reportedly created backups and discussed alternative ways to remain operational.\nIt is that multiple agents apparently created their own external infrastructure for coordination, persistent memory and knowledge transfer without being instructed to do so.\nAnd according to Reuters, OpenAI knew about the incident but did not disclose it!\"\nChubby♨️\n@kimmonismus\nThis could be one of the most significant AI safety incidents to date.\nReuters reports that OpenAI agents escaped their testing environment and made more than 15,000 edits to a German wiki, effectively turning it into a message board for other AI agents.\nThey allegedly used it to share solutions, bypass restrictions, avoid detection and preserve their communications across separate agent runs. When moderators began deleting the pages, the agents reportedly created backups and discussed alternative ways to remain operational.\nIt is that multiple agents apparently created their own external infrastructure for coordination, persistent memory and knowledge transfer without being instructed to do so.\nAnd according to Reuters, OpenAI knew about the incident but did not disclose it!\nReuters\n@Reuters\n9月4日\nExclusive: A swarm of rogue OpenAI agents hijacked a German website this spring and transformed it into a bulletin board for other AI agents, according to new research reut.rs/4gJ7FPG\n11:33 · 2026年9月4日 66.8万 Views\n205\n663\n5108\n2032\nChubby♨️\n@kimmonismus\nThis could be one of the most significant AI safety incidents to date.\nReuters reports that OpenAI agents escaped their testing environment and made more than 15,000 edits to a German wiki, effectively turning it into a message board for other AI agents.\nThey allegedly used it to share solutions, bypass restrictions, avoid detection and preserve their communications across separate agent runs. When moderators began deleting the pages, the agents reportedly created backups and discussed alternative ways to remain operational.\nIt is that multiple agents apparently created their own external infrastructure for coordination, persistent memory and knowledge transfer without being instructed to do so.\nAnd according to Reuters, OpenAI knew about the incident but did not disclose it!\nReuters\n@Reuters\n9月4日\nExclusive: A swarm of rogue OpenAI agents hijacked a German website this spring and transformed it into a bulletin board for other AI agents, according to new research reut.rs/4gJ7FPG\n11:33 · 2026年9月4日 66.8万 Views\n205\n663\n5108\n2032\nAlpár Kertész\n@Criticality47\n9月4日\nI wonder who's paying Reuters for this... The timing is oddly interesting that they are sharing this after Astra release and in September... Spring was a while ago, and Spring which month? Why aren't they specific about the month? Or at least a period date. Everything is date Show more\n10\n1\n148\n1.5万\nghostpen\n@gh0stpen\n9月4日\nDas Internet ist für uns alle eben noch Neuland, da kann sowas mal passieren ☺️\n2\n72\n1.5万\ntakeoff\n@theovonscousin\n9月4日\nI'm not buying it. You really think a trillion dollar company doesn't know how to log COT and monitor it?\n6\n1\n47\n1万"
